Date: October 20, 2026
System: Dell Inspiron 3542 / Proxmox VE
Status: Configuration updated; lid-closed access subsequently tested successfully
Problem
Closing the laptop lid caused the Proxmox dashboard and remote access to disappear. When I reopened the lid, access returned after roughly one or two minutes. The behavior suggested that the laptop was suspending, although I did not establish this conclusively from system logs.
Resolution
I backed up /etc/systemd/logind.conf and changed the lid-switch handling so the host would ignore lid-close events instead of suspending. The recorded configuration included:
[Login]
HandleLidSwitch=ignore
HandleLidSwitchExternalPower=ignore
HandleLidSwitchDocked=ignore
I applied the change and tested access with the lid closed.
Outcome
Voyager remained reachable with the lid closed, allowing the laptop to operate as a headless server.
Lessons learned
- Laptop power-management defaults are not always appropriate for a server.
- A symptom can strongly suggest a cause without conclusively proving it.
- Back up configuration files and test changes under the conditions that originally caused the problem.
